# nostromo_access.py

I enjoyed writing this program, and recreating a scene from the movie Alien (1979).

# Program Logic

## Declarations

random was imported to facilitate simulated logins

Two separate functions were declared (adminQuery() and userQuery()). Each function returns a doc string only meant for either an 'admin' or 'user' respectively.

Roles were assigned with the 'role' attribute in the class 'Crew'. Two class instances were declared admin_science_officer, and user_warrant_officer. admin_science_officer was assigned role 'admin', and user_warrant_officer was assigned role 'user'

## Simulated login

Next a list 'nostromo_compliment' was declared and populated with user_warrant_officer, and admin_science_officer.
simulated_logged_user used random.choice to parse list nostromo_compliment, the class instance it retrued becomes the logged in user Ash or Ripley.

Lastly an if/elif/else structure was used to determine if the Crew class instance roles == 'admin' or 'user'. If 'user' function userQuery() was returned, else if 'admin' adminQuery() was returned. Otherwise if data was tampered with, 'UNABLE TO COMPUTE' was retruned, and data remained confidential.
